{"authors": [], "discovered_at": "2026-10-13T03:28:59.195173Z", "id": "github:release:535360445:release:410964449", "kind": "release", "matched_terms": [], "metadata": {"action": "released", "draft": false, "forks": 11850, "prerelease": false, "stars": 62437, "stars_delta": 45, "tag_name": "v8.4.176"}, "organization": "ultralytics", "priority": {"source": 0.5}, "published_at": "2026-10-12T20:13:57Z", "related_items": [], "scores": {}, "source": "github", "source_id": "535360445:release:410964449", "summary": "## \ud83c\udf1f Summary\nYOLO 8.4.176 makes YOLO-World checkpoints much smaller after setting custom classes, while improving reliability across validation, fine-tuning, segmentation, tracking, and model deployment.\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Key Changes\n- **YOLO-World checkpoints are dramatically smaller:** Setting classes no longer caches the CLIP text encoder by default. For `yolov8s-worldv2.pt`, a saved checkpoint shrank from **328.5 MB to 25.8 MB**, with identical predictions after reload. Caching remains available when explicitly requested.\n- **More reliable validation and fine-tuning:** Detection validation now matches predictions to eligible targets in confidence order, reducing missed matches. YOLOE fine-tuning and resume also preserve trained classification heads instead of reinitializing them.\n- **Fixes for segmentation and SAM:** MobileSAM FP16 inference no longer produces empty masks. Reused SAM predictors now reset state for new images and videos. A mask-thresholding change was reverted after it reduced YOLO26 segmentation mAP.\n- **Improved deployment and input handling:** ONNX GPU inference now supports custom input names and strided tensors; OpenVINO NPU inference handles batches and depth outputs more reliably. Floating-point NumPy images also work with grayscale models.\n- **Smoother video, tracking, and benchmarking:** Saved videos preserve fractional frame rates, high-FPS streams are handled correctly, and trackers can be copied or pickled on newer Python versions. Several benchmark workflow issues were fixed.\n- **Documentation and Platform updates:** Docs clarify fine-tuning, inference, and precision behavior; Platform documentation covers relevance-based dataset sorting, email changes, and AI-assisted model comparison.\n\n## \ud83c\udfaf Purpose & Impact\n- **Save storage and simplify sharing:** YOLO-World users can save and move custom-vocabulary checkpoints without carrying an unnecessary CLIP encoder.\n- **Trust results and continue training safely:** Validation matching and YOLOE resume fixes reduce misleading evaluation results and prevent trained heads from being lost.\n- **Get more dependable inference across devices:** SAM, ONNX, OpenVINO, image inputs, and video handling work more consistently across common workflows.\n- **Keep segmentation metrics stable:** Reverting the mask threshold avoids the measured mAP regression introduced by the earlier change.\n\n## What's Changed\n* Threshold rescaled segment val masks and keep saved video duration with vid_stride by @Nicholas022400701 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26416\n* Add Hailo-8 benchmarks picture to doc by @lakshanthad in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26615\n* Fix confidence-ordered validation matching for alternate targets by @Nikhi00718 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26616\n* Preserve ONNX input names and values in GPU binding by @aswanth-07 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26618\n* Fix empty MobileSAM masks in FP16 by computing LayerNorm2d with the native kernel by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26639\n* Revert segment val mask thresholding from #26416 by @Laughing-q in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26645\n* Make per-tracker track ID counters picklable on Python 3.14 by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26638\n* Reset SAM predictor state for every new source by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26644\n* Fix legacy precision flags, used models and repeat directory runs in benchmarks by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26640\n* Sync docs with recent precision, preprocessing, finetuning and Platform changes by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26633\n* Accept floating NumPy color images for grayscale models by @aswanth-07 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26632\n* Pin torch when auto-installing nvidia-modelopt for TensorRT 11 export by @Zephyr4772 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26624\n* Fix channel swap in ReID crops passed to embedding models by @cainiao33 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26628\n* Fix OpenVINO NPU batch and depth inference by @onuralpszr in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26641\n* Keep the fused YOLOE head when resuming or re-fine-tuning PE checkpoints by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26646\n* Preserve fractional and high FPS in saved videos and stream loaders by @Vaishnavi220506 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26627\n* Reseed Albumentations in each DataLoader worker by @8rulerstar in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26635\n* Preserve non-ASCII class names and paths in Windows logs by @Nikhi00718 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26626\n* `ultralytics 8.4.176` Keep CLIP out of YOLO-World checkpoints after set_classes (328 MB \u2192 26 MB) by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26647\n\n## New Contributors\n* @Zephyr4772 made their first contribution in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26624\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/compare/v8.4.175...v8.4.176\n", "title": "ultralytics/ultralytics v8.4.176 - `ultralytics 8.4.176` Keep CLIP out of YOLO-World checkpoints after set_classes (328 MB \u2192 26 MB) (#26647)", "topics": 